# Update documentation with every change

When you implement a feature, enhancement, bug fix that changes behavior, API, roles, data model, or user-visible flow, **update the matching docs in the same work** — do not leave documentation for a follow-up unless the user explicitly says so.

## Which docs to touch

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| New/changed capability, acceptance, roles, NFR | [`docs/FRD.md`](docs/FRD.md) — add/revise `FR-*` / `NFR-*` + AC |
| Flows, business rules, screens, APIs, entities, integrations | [`docs/FSD.md`](docs/FSD.md) — module section + FR→FSD traceability |
| Schema fields / enums / FK map | [`docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md`](docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md) |
| Relationships / ER visuals | [`docs/ER_DIAGRAMS.md`](docs/ER_DIAGRAMS.md) |
| Staff-facing how-to / nav / day-to-day flow | [`docs/USER_GUIDE.md`](docs/USER_GUIDE.md) |
| Go-live, env vars, deploy, scheduler/SMTP ops | [`packaging/GO-LIVE-NOTES.md`](packaging/GO-LIVE-NOTES.md) and/or [`.env.example`](.env.example) |
| Doc index / export commands | [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md) only if needed |

Skip doc updates for pure refactors, typo-only edits, or internal cleanups with **no** behavior, API, schema, or UX change.

## How to update

1. Prefer editing **Markdown sources** (`FRD.md`, `FSD.md`, `DATA_DICTIONARY.md`, `ER_DIAGRAMS.md`, `USER_GUIDE.md`) — they are the source of truth.
2. Keep FRD = WHAT/WHO/AC; FSD = HOW; DATA_DICTIONARY = fields; ER_DIAGRAMS = visuals; USER_GUIDE = operate the UI. Do not duplicate full API tables into the FRD.
3. Mark feature-flagged / off-by-default items as optional — do not invent unbuilt roadmap features.
4. After substantive doc edits (especially Mermaid), regenerate Word/PDF when practical:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/export-doc.ps1 -DocName FRD -Title "Hardware Inventory - Functional Requirements Document"
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/export-doc.ps1 -DocName FSD -Title "Hardware Inventory - Functional Specification Document"
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/export-doc.ps1 -DocName DATA_DICTIONARY -Title "Hardware Inventory - Data Dictionary"
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/export-doc.ps1 -DocName ER_DIAGRAMS -Title "Hardware Inventory - ER Diagrams"
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/export-user-guide.ps1
```

If Pandoc/Chrome is unavailable, still update the `.md` files and note that exports were skipped.

## Done check

Before finishing a behavior-changing task: docs reflect the change, requirement IDs/traceability still make sense, and the user-facing guide is not stale for that module.
